Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.21,0:00:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I should begin by saying
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.79,0:00:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,what an honor it is\Nto make your acquaintance.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.33,0:00:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I've read all about your games.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.00,0:00:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Very impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.42,0:00:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a shame
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.04,0:00:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,to leave a mind as brilliant as yours\Nrotting in such a hole.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.50,0:00:55.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Down!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.00,0:01:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,There are very few who have such power\Nto lever you out of this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.58,0:01:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I am among one such group of individuals.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.04,0:01:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,We can make it look like you escaped.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.58,0:01:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Many years ago,\Nsome items of worth were misplaced.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.79,0:01:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,We want them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.04,0:01:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Help us and you will be free.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.63,0:01:29.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Does the name
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.38,0:01:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.25,0:01:33.58,Default,,0,0,0,,mean anything to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.79,0:01:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I read somewhere that\Nall good stories begin with a wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.08,0:01:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is she?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.75,0:01:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,This one certainly does.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.50,0:02:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,She's very late.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.88,0:02:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone's approaching.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.33,0:02:11.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.33,0:02:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.58,0:02:21.75,Default,,0,0,0,,-Oh.\N-Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.08,0:02:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Regrettably, however, this wedding\Nis lacking one crucial element.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.75,0:02:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,'Tis I.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.42,0:02:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.71,0:02:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, the bride in question\Nis having doubts
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.04,0:02:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,about what it means to become a lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.58,0:02:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't touch the ginger cake.\NPlays hopscotch with your bowels.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.04,0:02:49.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.96,0:02:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady Enola Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.83,0:02:53.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't sound right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.92,0:02:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.42,0:02:58.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I've spent the six years making\Nmyself feel worthy of the Holmes name.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.21,0:03:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Would I now be giving that up?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.75,0:03:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And as I was once told by a wise woman…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.79,0:03:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,-Well, not a wise woman. My mother.\N-There are two paths you can take, Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.71,0:03:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Yours, or the path others choose for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.04,0:03:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.13,0:03:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Ow! Will you stop that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.75,0:03:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot leave him there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.50,0:03:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.17,0:03:25.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Coachman Eric? Coachman Eric?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.33,0:03:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you'd scarpered.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.79,0:03:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Has Sherlock gone ahead?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.92,0:03:30.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Darling girl,\Neveryone's at your wedding, bar you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.50,0:03:32.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-Now, are you ready to go?\N-Yes, yes, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.13,0:03:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yah, yah!\N-Fast as you can!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.46,0:03:43.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Now might be a good time\Nto tell you my wedding is in Malta,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.08,0:03:46.58,Default,,0,0,0,,the small island in the Mediterranean Sea,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.08,0:03:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,for reasons that are complicated\Nto understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.88,0:03:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-She'll be here, don't worry.\N-Yes, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.96,0:03:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yah! Yah!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.13,0:04:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, madam.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.00,0:04:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,To concern you a little,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.33,0:04:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,we have a man in pursuit.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.75,0:04:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,He does not look savory.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.50,0:04:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Highwaymen, vagabonds, thieves!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.50,0:04:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Malta has more than its fair share.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.88,0:04:17.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Yah! Yah!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.04,0:04:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.63,0:04:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep down! Keep down, madam!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.17,0:04:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-This is no place for a lady!\N-I'm not a lady yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.54,0:04:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,-Quicker!\N-Here, take this!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.17,0:04:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam, what are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.38,0:04:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Come down from up there!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.46,0:04:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola! It's me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.08,0:04:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.46,0:05:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola, are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.58,0:05:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Why were you wearing a mask?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.79,0:05:07.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's a handkerchief.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.25,0:05:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The dust plays havoc with my lungs.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.75,0:05:12.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-You thought I was--\N-Murdering me?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.54,0:05:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-No.\N-Yes, that's exactly what I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.67,0:05:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Why were you pursuing me?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.83,0:05:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.63,0:05:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He's missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.13,0:05:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, I'm more or less certain, Enola,\Nthat Sherlock has been kidnapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.88,0:05:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.21,0:05:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand you may need\Nsome explanation as to how this all began.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.25,0:05:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The truth is,\Nwe had our lives exactly as we wanted.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.75,0:05:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury continued to be the champion\Nfor change and progress,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.71,0:05:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,and I had finally joined the pantheon\Nof great Victorian detectives,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.71,0:05:45.92,Default,,0,0,0,,alongside my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.54,0:05:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,He helped those with means,\Nand I helped those with needs.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.75,0:05:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And on occasion, we worked together.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.42,0:05:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I was happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.92,0:05:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And here, the trail runs cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.75,0:06:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't come any further.\NWe have to keep it as clear as we can.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.96,0:06:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,A horse was mounted.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.08,0:06:06.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-And the man made his departure this way.\N-A good suggestion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.13,0:06:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You have another?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.29,0:06:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The man was lassoed by a noose\Nand hanged from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.25,0:06:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you see the rope remnants\Nthat have not been fully cut away?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.79,0:06:17.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And the marks here,\Nwhere flailing feet aimed for purchase.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.96,0:06:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock, this is not\Nwhere the man disappeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.88,0:06:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a murder scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.88,0:06:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,-Is that Sherlock Holmes?\N-They're less fun than you'd think.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.83,0:06:27.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Detection filled my weeks,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.46,0:06:30.42,Default,,0,0,0,,and on the weekends were, well…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.21,0:06:32.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury, what are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.96,0:06:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Got a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.46,0:06:35.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Flowers?\N-No.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.79,0:06:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Herbs?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.88,0:06:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Close your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.04,0:06:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.83,0:06:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,What have you found?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.00,0:06:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-Oh!\N-I just found him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.33,0:06:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-Sweet boy.\N-Can you believe it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.33,0:06:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.25,0:06:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,-It was glorious.\N-He's a bit shy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.00,0:06:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It was fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.83,0:06:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,When it was neither fun nor glorious,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.25,0:06:59.88,Default,,0,0,0,,when it was just the two of us,\Nthose were the best times of all.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.96,0:07:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Back. And when I go in,\Nyou back against that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.63,0:07:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Tewkesbury. Tewkesbury!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.46,0:07:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,So whilst my life\Nseemed completely uncomplicated,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.58,0:07:17.08,Default,,0,0,0,,my dear, dear lord\Ndecided to add a slight complication.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.29,0:07:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola Eudoria Holmes,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.13,0:07:22.46,Default,,0,0,0,,uh, will you take I,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.38,0:07:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Earnest Augustus\Nof the House of Tewkesbury…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.63,0:07:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.54,0:07:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,He has a first name.\NI… I was surprised too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.04,0:07:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,…to be your husband?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.79,0:07:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Read all about it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.13,0:07:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Suddenly, we had the attention\Nof the whole of London.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.29,0:07:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,-Delightful.\N-Ravishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.38,0:07:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, except for one person.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.96,0:07:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.13,0:07:56.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The world's most famous detective\Nhad become obsessed with something.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.83,0:07:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello, Sherlock.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.67,0:08:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It was all maps and symbols,\Nand nothing I could make any sense of.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.88,0:08:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn't understand\Nwhy he was keeping it from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.75,0:08:12.46,Default,,0,0,0,,On the flowers…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.54,0:08:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,-We did discuss chrysanthemums.\N-Chrysanthemums?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.83,0:08:18.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes! They're my favorite.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.83,0:08:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What's next? Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.04,0:08:23.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I have prepared a short list\Nof our nearest and dearest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.46,0:08:26.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I do, uh, have one myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.42,0:08:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I borrow your pen?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.46,0:08:30.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Just one more person.\NShe won't be able to make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.75,0:08:32.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.88,0:08:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,No room for your mother?\NShe will be quite welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.13,0:08:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Since the passing\Nof the Explosive Substances Act of 1883,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.25,0:08:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,my mother has become a…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.17,0:08:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,…fugitive of the first class.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.13,0:08:57.50,Default,,0,0,0,,So attending\Na well-advertised ceremony such as this
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.58,0:08:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,would compromise her safety
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.46,0:09:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,greatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.42,0:09:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Might there be an uncle…
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.46,0:09:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Mother.\N-…who might walk you down the aisle?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.50,0:09:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I spoke with Sherlock…
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.92,0:09:13.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Ta-da.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.42,0:09:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,…and he consented to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.79,0:09:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,-He will?\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.88,0:09:19.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.83,0:09:21.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And so he will do so curmudgeonly,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.96,0:09:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,and he will lack elegance\Nand a sense of life behind his eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.00,0:09:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,but he is all I have, so it will be great.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.58,0:09:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, not all will attend\Non Earnest's side.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.50,0:09:33.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He is well-loved, but…
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.46,0:09:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Given the family's history,\NI presume the wedding will be in Malta?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.25,0:09:38.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Malta.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.21,0:09:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Malta?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.13,0:09:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Where on earth has that come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.08,0:09:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I was taking tea with the ladies,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.42,0:09:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and of course the wedding\Nwas the talk of the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.58,0:09:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,When the topic moved on\Nto the matter of the venue,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.92,0:09:56.08,Default,,0,0,0,,one of the ladies asked\Nwhere Peter and I were wed,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.17,0:09:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and I thought it just wonderful.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.00,0:09:59.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Malta.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.96,0:10:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,What better way to honor your father?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.42,0:10:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-I'm sorry.\N-It was my husband's delight.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.58,0:10:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,His time in the military\Nwas spent there, we met there,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.33,0:10:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,we married there.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.33,0:10:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And Earnest deeply loved\Nhis childhood summers there.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.83,0:10:14.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.13,0:10:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, if you wish to do it elsewhere,\Nthat is the bride's prerogative.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.00,0:10:26.33,Default,,0,0,0,,My wedding in Malta?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.83,0:10:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I had so many questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.79,0:10:30.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What does one wear to a Maltese wedding?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.58,0:10:33.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Do I know anyone in Malta?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.33,0:10:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps you're free this Saturday.\NAre you free this Saturday?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.00,0:10:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Pretend to be my great-great-grandmother.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.75,0:10:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,More importantly,\Nhow did Sherlock know before I did?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.63,0:10:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And why was he so concerned?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.50,0:10:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Pay attention, Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.33,0:10:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's what my mother taught me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.21,0:10:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Though but a speck\Nin the Mediterranean Sea,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.63,0:10:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Malta has been invaded by the Phoenicians,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.21,0:10:54.63,Default,,0,0,0,,the Romans, and even Napoleon,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.71,0:10:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,for its strategic importance.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.54,0:10:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Since 1814,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.75,0:11:01.04,Default,,0,0,0,,the island has been under military control\Nof the British Empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.13,0:11:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.04,0:11:03.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.00,0:11:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Before I knew it, the wedding was upon us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.04,0:11:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And that is how we found ourselves
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.54,0:11:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,in a room packed full\Nof the great and the good.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.75,0:11:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,His family, delighted the young viscount\Nhad finally settled on a bride,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.79,0:11:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,and my family,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.92,0:11:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,well, behaving\Nin a more complicated manner.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.75,0:11:24.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Were no more of your family\Nable to join for the wedding party?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.83,0:11:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.04,0:11:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.00,0:11:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Ladies and gentlemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.50,0:11:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,as the British governor\Nof this beautiful province,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.67,0:11:37.88,Default,,0,0,0,,it is my honor\Nto invite our great defender,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.96,0:11:40.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Brigadier General Sampson,\Nto make a toast.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.25,0:11:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Brigadier General!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.21,0:11:43.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll meet him. He's great.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.54,0:11:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, everyone. Thank you. Uh…
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.25,0:11:47.96,Default,,0,0,0,,As godfather to the groom,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.04,0:11:52.29,Default,,0,0,0,,it is an honor and delight\Nto make tonight's toast.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.38,0:11:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my friend, uh, Lord Tewkesbury,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.29,0:11:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,uh, Peter,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.04,0:11:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,was a proud father,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.25,0:12:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,and he saw in his son\Nan opportunity to make a man.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.04,0:12:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And what Earnest has shown us
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.29,0:12:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,since his ascension to the House of Lords
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.75,0:12:08.88,Default,,0,0,0,,has been most distinguished.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.46,0:12:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Young revolutionary\Nprepared to stand side by side
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.50,0:12:14.75,Default,,0,0,0,,with those less fortunate
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.83,0:12:18.71,Default,,0,0,0,,and see them almost as equals.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.29,0:12:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Which, uh, perhaps explains\Nhis choice of bride.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.92,0:12:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I jest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.08,0:12:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Forgive me, I jest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.75,0:12:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, uh, she's quite\Na remarkable young woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.42,0:12:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,As is my godson,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.08,0:12:36.96,Default,,0,0,0,,a, well, a remarkable young man.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.67,0:12:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,What a couple they will make.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.63,0:12:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Ladies and gentlemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.33,0:12:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,would you please be upstanding?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.21,0:12:49.33,Default,,0,0,0,,If you'll excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.42,0:12:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I give you…
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.50,0:12:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry,\NI don't know what that was about.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.50,0:12:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,…the happy couple.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.79,0:12:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-The happy couple.\N-The happy couple.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.42,0:13:12.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.42,0:13:14.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Where have you been?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.46,0:13:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,That is none of your concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.13,0:13:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What business have you in Malta?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.88,0:13:21.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this a new case?\NAnd if so, why wouldn't you include me?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.50,0:13:22.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is that man you were watching?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.04,0:13:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola, I'm tired.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.67,0:13:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Or are you simply\Njust distracting yourself
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.46,0:13:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,from the boredom of watching your sister\Ncommit to something you have no stake in?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.71,0:13:34.29,Default,,0,0,0,,-Oh, it is I that is seeking distraction?\N-You are making a judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.21,0:13:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,It is not a subtle one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.46,0:13:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not blame you for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.21,0:13:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,If I were in your situation,\NI would seek distraction too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.00,0:13:45.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would you give away\Nyour freedom to these people?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.46,0:13:48.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I am not giving away freedom.\NI am simply marrying a lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.42,0:13:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,-I knew what I was getting myself into.\N-What could tempt you to be predictable?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.88,0:13:53.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course you can't understand\Nan act of love.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.71,0:13:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What can marriage offer\Na mind such as yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.67,0:13:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You give up your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.42,0:13:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Your standing as a detective.\N-I will keep working.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.79,0:14:02.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Take on title and tradition\Nyou cannot understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.13,0:14:04.88,Default,,0,0,0,,No. You are better than that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.46,0:14:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.79,0:14:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And what good is that name?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.08,0:14:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My father's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.25,0:14:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My eldest brother a bore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.13,0:14:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother, a stick of dynamite\Nlong since exploded.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.00,0:14:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And all that's left is you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.96,0:14:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And if this is how you choose to love me,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.92,0:14:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,then I would rather\Nlose my name for eternity.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.17,0:14:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You're being emotional.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.46,0:14:48.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand that you are upset,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.25,0:14:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,but I am also right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.00,0:14:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You have compromised yourself fatally.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.21,0:14:56.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I am not so frightened of society
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.21,0:14:58.33,Default,,0,0,0,,that I will not conform\Nto its wishes occasionally.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.92,0:15:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury needs to be married.\NSo I will… I must marry--
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.92,0:15:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Do as you are told?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.21,0:15:05.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.54,0:15:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a pig, Sherlock Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.58,0:15:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,This pig would like some peace and quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.63,0:15:18.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That was the last time I saw him.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.08,0:15:20.42,Default,,0,0,0,,But Sherlock Holmes
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.21,0:15:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,kidnapped?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.88,0:15:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.08,0:15:29.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not only possible,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.88,0:15:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,but probable.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.46,0:15:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-Interesting.\N-What's interesting?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.38,0:15:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The room has been torn apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.54,0:15:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.21,0:15:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,it looks perfectly normal to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.96,0:15:45.92,Default,,0,0,0,,His garments have been left untouched,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.00,0:15:49.08,Default,,0,0,0,,so whoever did this\Nknows he cares nothing for them,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.17,0:15:52.46,Default,,0,0,0,,which means whoever did this\Nhas some knowledge of my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.67,0:15:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's warm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.83,0:16:00.88,Default,,0,0,0,,He was taken within the last few hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.71,0:16:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,He was smoking Bristol tobacco.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.42,0:16:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Not his usual shag.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.29,0:16:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,His notebooks.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.29,0:16:15.46,Default,,0,0,0,,A testing code.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.38,0:16:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I will break it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.54,0:16:24.29,Default,,0,0,0,,-What case were you working on here?\N-In Malta?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.79,0:16:26.83,Default,,0,0,0,,No case. We're here for your wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.92,0:16:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,But last night at the banquet,\Nhe was watching someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.38,0:16:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Case?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.13,0:16:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,-What case? Why did I not know of this--\N-Stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.04,0:16:49.21,Default,,0,0,0,,A Holmes does not disappear\Nwithout leaving clues for a Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.96,0:16:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Other detectives may be available.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.29,0:16:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother has left his mark somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.71,0:16:56.83,Default,,0,0,0,,What if he hasn't?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.92,0:16:59.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you do not know my brother at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.42,0:17:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I care for him too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.29,0:17:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.50,0:17:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.58,0:17:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You're scared. We both are.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.75,0:17:14.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not doubt Sherlock has doubted me,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.04,0:17:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,but he must have left me something.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.08,0:17:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's keep looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.46,0:17:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,K-H…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.75,0:17:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,O…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.08,0:17:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,S-T?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.92,0:17:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Khost?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.63,0:17:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. Isn't that a city in--
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.13,0:17:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,In Afghanistan, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.46,0:17:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where are you seeing this?\N-On the mirror.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.96,0:17:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-On the mirror?\N-Mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.50,0:17:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Might they just be signs of a struggle?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.71,0:18:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,No, that's Morse code.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.88,0:18:08.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.46,0:18:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,whilst he was being taken,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.79,0:18:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,he was dragged out and left this for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.71,0:18:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Khost?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.13,0:18:27.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.33,0:18:31.71,Default,,0,0,0,,They're returning.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.29,0:18:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The wedding party.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.25,0:18:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he needs to understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.13,0:18:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Off we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.08,0:18:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Surprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.54,0:19:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The audacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.46,0:19:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Absolute disgrace.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.88,0:19:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not the most popular soul\Nin Malta right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.71,0:19:08.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Understandably.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.33,0:19:12.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But he will understand when I tell him\Nof Sherlock's disappearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.21,0:19:26.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Pull on every loose thread you find.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.58,0:19:33.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury will understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.71,0:19:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.75,0:19:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,But I cannot let him escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.71,0:19:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a clue. As my mother taught me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.58,0:19:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,when you're solving a mystery,\Nyou pull on a ball of thread.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.71,0:19:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm losing my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.04,0:19:50.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Coming through!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.63,0:19:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,No, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.58,0:19:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.25,0:19:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Move, move, move!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.29,0:19:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Terribly sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.13,0:20:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,-Move!\N-Just stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.42,0:20:01.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.38,0:20:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.75,0:20:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop him!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.83,0:20:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.00,0:20:16.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Make way!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.04,0:20:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Make way!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.96,0:20:20.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Move!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.17,0:20:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.63,0:20:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me. I will find you help.\NPlease, just tell me your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.54,0:20:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where's my brother? Where's my brother?\N-Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.08,0:20:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrath?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.63,0:20:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What's "wrath"?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.58,0:20:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.83,0:20:54.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What's "wrath"? Sir, wake up!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.38,0:20:57.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Wake up. What's "wrath"?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.17,0:21:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, somebody help!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.75,0:21:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Look for what's there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.08,0:21:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Not what you want to be there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.67,0:21:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll see the truth soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.50,0:21:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother is missing,\Nand the man he was pursuing, dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.29,0:21:31.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Why was Sherlock\Nsuspicious of that sergeant?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.83,0:21:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Why was he killed?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.00,0:21:34.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.25,0:21:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And by who?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.46,0:21:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all connected.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.00,0:21:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,But at this stage, I don't know how.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.67,0:21:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,All I really have are two words.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.42,0:21:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Khost, we know.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.71,0:21:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But what of wrath?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.92,0:21:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Another place?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.58,0:21:50.79,Default,,0,0,0,,A person?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.29,0:21:53.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps Sherlock knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.04,0:21:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,His notebooks.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.67,0:21:58.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course he wrote them in code.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.38,0:22:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you forget\NI, too, was raised on ciphers.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.08,0:22:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Two five-letter words.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.83,0:22:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The fourth letter in the first\Nmatches the last letter in the second.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.50,0:22:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Khost. Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.00,0:22:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-Agh!\N-Oh dear!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.00,0:22:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.83,0:22:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-Good grief, Enola!\N-Oh my!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.67,0:22:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-I hadn't even knocked, and you're--\N-It was a scary shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.50,0:22:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it bleeding?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.67,0:22:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yes, very much.\N-For goodness' sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.25,0:22:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-Can I see it?\N-No, just--
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.33,0:22:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it broken?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.25,0:23:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-No, just let me--\N-If you wiggle your nose--
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.75,0:23:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Shh!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.04,0:23:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Your poor nose.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.46,0:23:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Can I just take a look at your nose?\N-Whoa.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.08,0:23:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that your blood?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.08,0:23:18.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-No.\N-Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.33,0:23:20.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-No, it's the blood of another.\N-Oh, good.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.67,0:23:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,In any other hands,\Nthat would be horrifying to hear.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.96,0:23:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,With yours, it's a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.38,0:23:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-Well?\N-Sherlock is missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.54,0:23:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.96,0:23:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.25,0:23:48.63,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not how I imagined this moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.71,0:23:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,In truth,\Nthis is not how I imagined this day.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.13,0:23:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I was on my way to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.33,0:24:02.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I was traveling at great speed,\Nand then Dr. Watson was following me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.38,0:24:04.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought he was a highwayman,\Nso I tried to shoot at him,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.83,0:24:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,hence the state of my dress--
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.25,0:24:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me play detective for once.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.21,0:24:12.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Why were you traveling at great speed?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.21,0:24:13.04,Default,,0,0,0,,To be with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.13,0:24:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You were already late.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.58,0:24:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,To your own wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.75,0:24:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Your doubts about this\Nhave been clear for some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.13,0:24:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,-Tewkesbury--\N-No, don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.63,0:24:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I am sorry for any pain I have caused you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.00,0:24:35.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I truly hope you succeed\Nin finding your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.50,0:24:38.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure you will.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.29,0:25:01.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps my mother was right.\NI am meant to be alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.54,0:25:05.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna do very well\Non your own, Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.71,0:25:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the place he took me to\Nwhen we first arrived here.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.25,0:25:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,This is where Father and I\Nspent all our summers.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.63,0:25:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-You see that cave?\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.67,0:25:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,He told me when I was a boy\Nthat there was treasure hidden inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.33,0:25:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,So every summer,\NI'd ask him to take me to that cave,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.83,0:25:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,and we would strike matches.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.42,0:25:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We'd walk into the darkness together,\Npretending to be pirates or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.08,0:25:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, matey.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.50,0:25:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember vividly\Nmy heart beating like mad,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.75,0:25:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,truly thinking\Nwe might find a chest or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.79,0:25:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I did adore his stories though.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.46,0:25:48.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.04,0:25:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Times spent here,\Nthey were some of the happiest of my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.29,0:26:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I did not mean to hurt him.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.17,0:26:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not know if I can solve this case.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.50,0:26:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But if whoever this is\Nwill kill a man to protect their identity…
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.96,0:26:19.21,Default,,0,0,0,,what will they do to my brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.08,0:26:51.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.67,0:26:53.88,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.75,0:27:00.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury! Tewkesbury!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.71,0:27:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where's Tewkesbury?\N-He… he went inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.08,0:27:05.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-No!\N-He was looking for his mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.21,0:27:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We tried to stop him!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.21,0:27:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola, stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.21,0:27:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother! Are you there?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.50,0:27:25.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-Tewkesbury!\N-Over here!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.04,0:27:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.08,0:27:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.17,0:27:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.08,0:27:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.38,0:27:54.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-Mother!\N-Tewkesbury!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.75,0:27:58.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.46,0:28:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury. We have to go. She's not here.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.00,0:28:04.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-Nobody's seen her.\N-We have to go, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.96,0:28:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,No. Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.42,0:28:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury, did you force the door\Nwhen you came in here?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.08,0:28:12.21,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.08,0:28:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.38,0:28:18.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Mother!\N-Tewkesbury, look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.50,0:28:20.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-She has been kidnapped.\N-What?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.17,0:28:22.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to leave. We have to go right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.75,0:28:23.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.50,0:28:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.79,0:28:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Deep breath.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.88,0:28:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And again.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.58,0:28:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,One more.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.50,0:28:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.75,0:28:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.58,0:28:46.29,Default,,0,0,0,,you sound fine,\Nthough you may not feel that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.83,0:28:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would somebody take his mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.50,0:28:57.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.42,0:28:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,what would my brother do?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.21,0:29:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Deep breath.\N-Ouch!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.79,0:29:04.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not a detective.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.29,0:29:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, when I first moved in,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.08,0:29:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,he didn't know what to make of me,\Nif you can imagine that.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.88,0:29:13.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But I hoped we could be friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.46,0:29:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,so every day at teatime,\NI'd prepare a tray
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.67,0:29:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'd ask him\Nhow his latest case was progressing.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.58,0:29:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,And every day…
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.13,0:29:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,…he wouldn't know how to respond.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.25,0:29:28.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd have thought a cup of tea\Nwas a gun to his head.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.96,0:29:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,He just… He couldn't… he couldn't\Nquite fathom why I might be curious.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.08,0:29:37.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And every day I tried.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.79,0:29:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, I thought,\N"It's making you unhappy, John. Let go."
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.96,0:29:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And then one day, I was sat by the fire,\Nfinishing some work of my own,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.63,0:29:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,and he appeared with a cup of tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:52.96,0:29:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Terrible tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.54,0:29:58.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm. Yes. Too much milk.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.67,0:30:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Far too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.75,0:30:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,But he sat down, and for the first time,\Nhe told me about his case,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.00,0:30:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,and I found myself inexorably drawn in.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.00,0:30:10.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What did he tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.25,0:30:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's between me and him\Nand my diaries.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.08,0:30:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,But…
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.92,0:30:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,…you asked me
Dialogue: 0,0:30:25.33,0:30:28.29,Default,,0,0,0,,what would Sherlock truly say\Nwere he here.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:31.67,0:30:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,He isn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.96,0:30:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:36.63,0:30:38.88,Default,,0,0,0,,He thinks your brain equal to his.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.38,0:30:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Dear Doctor, I hope he's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.13,0:30:52.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Try, Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:53.38,0:30:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Talk to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.13,0:31:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.92,0:31:15.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you think it was the same people\Nthat took Sherlock?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.71,0:31:17.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I am certain of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.38,0:31:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would they take my mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.92,0:31:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know. But I will find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.58,0:31:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you are capable of finding her,\Nbut she has not Sherlock's strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.75,0:31:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,She has always lived\Na very… cosseted life.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.42,0:31:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,When did you last see her?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:50.17,0:31:51.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I left her
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.42,0:31:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,at nine. I went to say goodnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.42,0:31:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,She offered me comfort.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.83,0:32:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything will be\Nmuch improved by morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.63,0:32:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,She was wearing a nightgown, Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.13,0:32:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot waste another moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.00,0:32:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to ask the brigadier for help.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.88,0:32:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What would my brother say?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.50,0:32:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,A lady would never leave\Nher room unaccompanied at that hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.50,0:32:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,She would have gone to sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.83,0:32:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I was also taken from my room.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.46,0:32:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,They risked much returning to the scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.33,0:32:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Then there is the fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.08,0:32:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Are we truly dealing with a kidnapper,\Na murderer, and an arsonist all in one?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.71,0:32:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You ask the wrong question. Go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.13,0:32:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did the kidnapper start the fire?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.67,0:32:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Precisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.04,0:33:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,This kidnapper was looking for something.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.50,0:33:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But whatever he was seeking,\Nhe did not find.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.42,0:33:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you cannot find an object…
Dialogue: 0,0:33:22.79,0:33:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Burn everything\Nso no one will find it either.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.29,0:33:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Focus, Enola. Make no mistake,\Nyou are racing for my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.33,0:33:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And possibly your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.33,0:33:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Medals.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.46,0:34:30.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.46,0:34:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-Hey, hey, hey, whoa, whoa. Easy.\N-Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.13,0:34:34.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.29,0:34:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not telling you.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.00,0:34:37.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where is Sherlock Holmes?\N-I do not know.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.79,0:34:39.54,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where is Sherlock Holmes?\N-I do not know.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.63,0:34:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where have you taken him?\N-I have not taken him.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:42.38,0:34:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I can assure you I am desperate enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.50,0:34:47.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, whoa, whoa.\NWell, that would be stupid.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.08,0:34:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,No, and you… you… you are not stupid.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.58,0:34:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, that was stupid.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.88,0:34:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.38,0:35:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.63,0:35:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You…
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.88,0:35:18.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, lady. Oh, oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:18.88,0:35:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Jeez, no! Ow, ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.96,0:35:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, all right. I…
Dialogue: 0,0:35:22.29,0:35:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe your brother was taken\Nby Professor Adeline Rathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.29,0:35:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.46,0:35:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,-Who is she?\N-What?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.92,0:35:28.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is she?!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.83,0:35:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I have been following you
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.63,0:35:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,in the hope that you might\Nfind a way to her that I have not.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.50,0:35:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,She's a ghost, and a brutal one.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:35.54,0:35:37.88,Default,,0,0,0,,She has the ear of the governor.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.46,0:35:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,She appeared a year ago,\Nhearing everything. We do not trust her.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:42.33,0:35:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,And this woman has taken my brother\Nand Lady Tewkesbury?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.67,0:35:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Please get off me.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.33,0:36:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:08.04,0:36:12.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My name is Mikiel Mizzi\Nof the Partito Anti-Riformista,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.25,0:36:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and we believe in a free Malta.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:17.13,0:36:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And we wish to be rid of your Crown.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.00,0:36:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Of your destruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.83,0:36:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Of using our soldiers\Nto fight your battles,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.83,0:36:27.04,Default,,0,0,0,,not caring if they live or die.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.13,0:36:31.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And your need to control a country\Nthat you know nothing about.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.71,0:36:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I know who you are, Enola Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.38,0:36:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a great detective.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.63,0:36:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Your brother--
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.96,0:36:47.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If the police catch me here,\Nthey will throw me in jail.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.50,0:36:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,-I have to go.\N-No, you have to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.38,0:36:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You will require my help again.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.75,0:36:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-I will require yours.\N-You can't go.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:52.25,0:36:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-Our paths will cross.\N-I have more questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.21,0:36:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be watching you. Goodbye, Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.21,0:37:04.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh…
Dialogue: 0,0:37:12.00,0:37:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We are aware of you, Miss Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.25,0:37:18.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Inspector Lestrade\Nhas been very useful to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.54,0:37:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,We told him you were troubling.\NHe said that is your way.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.29,0:37:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Troubling how?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:22.58,0:37:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,An eyewitness puts you next to a dead body\Nat the scene of a crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.00,0:37:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-The man was clearly shot from above.\N-A dead body you failed to report.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.04,0:37:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-Then we find you inside a police--\N-Sergeant, my brother is missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.21,0:37:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,My future mother-in-law is missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:36.67,0:37:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I am a detective,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.67,0:37:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,and I am trying to find the woman\Nheld responsible for all of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:41.13,0:37:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Which woman?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.88,0:37:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Professor Adeline Rathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.79,0:37:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Why might you be interested in--
Dialogue: 0,0:37:46.88,0:37:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-Sergeant Indri.\N-Yes, Governor.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.96,0:37:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,-You appear to have made a mistake.\N-Sir, I--
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.88,0:37:54.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You are here under a remit\Nfor Maltese crimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.46,0:37:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola Holmes is English.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.75,0:37:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,She is your better.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.75,0:38:01.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Oh, sir.\N-Uh, I do not think I am better. It--
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.50,0:38:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, respectfully, she is here\Nfor a criminal investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.38,0:38:07.83,Default,,0,0,0,,-I do not believe--\N-I do not care what you believe, Sergeant.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:10.92,0:38:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Holmes,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.92,0:38:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,you may leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.92,0:38:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again, Miss Holmes,\NI apologize for our misjudgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.63,0:38:28.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, sir. You've been a huge help.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.83,0:38:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Absolutely, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.08,0:38:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-What is this?\N-The summer carnival.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.54,0:38:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,How jolly.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.92,0:38:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-I did not like that any more than you.\N-Is that how people here are treated?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.96,0:38:42.33,Default,,0,0,0,,-It is the system.\N-The system is not serviceable.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.42,0:38:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Why was he so eager\Nfor me to stop speaking to the sergeant?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.38,0:38:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Also, I found these in your mother's room.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.63,0:38:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Whose are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:50.71,0:38:54.38,Default,,0,0,0,,These are my father's war medals.\NMaybe they were meant as a wedding gift?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.54,0:38:56.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.08,0:38:59.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you looking at?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.96,0:39:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.29,0:39:11.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-Wrath…\N-She has the ear of the governor.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.21,0:39:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.83,0:39:18.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-Tewkesbury, I have to go.\N-Enola-- Shall I join?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.29,0:39:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak to that sergeant.\NFind out what he knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:26.67,0:39:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Viva carnival!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.04,0:39:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.25,0:40:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.29,0:40:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.63,0:40:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.58,0:40:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.38,0:41:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:03.67,0:41:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You should not have followed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.42,0:41:07.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you Professor Adeline Rathe?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.83,0:41:08.88,Default,,0,0,0,,No. No.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.96,0:41:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-I need to know where my brother is.\N-You have made a mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.58,0:41:22.54,Default,,0,0,0,,-Look at me. I can help you.\N-She will kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.96,0:41:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-She will kill you.\N-Who will kill me?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.13,0:41:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is she?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:28.88,0:41:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me. Tell me! Please, tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.00,0:41:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Not again.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:34.00,0:41:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.29,0:42:04.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-Who is she?\N-She will kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.13,0:42:05.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hearing everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.75,0:42:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Ignored for years.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.50,0:42:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Playing them all.\N-It's all a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:13.29,0:42:14.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-She's having…\N-Fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:15.04,0:42:17.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps we shall take to the floor again.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.17,0:42:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We make it look like\Nyou escaped, Professor.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.83,0:42:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Moriarty.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.21,0:42:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What a clever girl you are, Enola Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.38,0:42:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.04,0:42:43.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is my brother? Is he dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:43.54,0:42:45.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he dead?!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.13,0:42:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.58,0:42:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It pleases me to keep him.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:48.54,0:42:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Though he has given up\Non hoping you will come to save him.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.96,0:42:59.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Why are you here?\N-Isn't this splendid?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:00.46,0:43:03.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The British government\Nare building Malta a sewage network.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:03.83,0:43:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,A wonderful place to hide.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:10.46,0:43:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, there's the matter\Nof the wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.67,0:43:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,With all those newspaper announcements,\Nyou practically invited me.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.50,0:43:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That sad expression on his face,\Nwaiting for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.25,0:43:26.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you get cold feet, Enola?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:28.00,0:43:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Though perhaps he deserved to suffer.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:37.71,0:43:39.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You came here to ruin my family?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:39.67,0:43:41.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Amongst other things, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:56.25,0:43:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You're further behind the curve\Nthan I thought, Detective Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:01.29,0:44:02.83,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.92,0:44:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Step away from my daughter!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:06.00,0:44:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother! Get off of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.58,0:44:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Eudoria Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:11.04,0:44:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-How delightful.\N-Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:13.92,0:44:14.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The pleasure's mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:15.04,0:44:17.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Your children vex me.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:17.21,0:44:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, they vex me too.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.13,0:44:43.21,Default,,0,0,0,,-You all right?\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.38,0:44:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,She's gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:49.96,0:44:51.17,Default,,0,0,0,,'Tis I.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:52.04,0:44:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, this is all a ridiculous merry mess.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:55.67,0:44:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Ridiculous is you being here, Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:58.71,0:45:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You walking away from me?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:00.50,0:45:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:01.83,0:45:03.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I have work to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.67,0:45:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother is missing,\Nmy soon-to-be mother-in-law is, and…
Dialogue: 0,0:45:09.25,0:45:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You have been absent for far too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.08,0:45:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:13.29,0:45:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I was here for your wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.63,0:45:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,One is a wanted woman.\NOne could hardly advertise it.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:21.04,0:45:25.04,Default,,0,0,0,,So you just expected to watch my wedding\Nin secret and then flee back to London?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:27.83,0:45:31.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-That sounds less romantic than I had it.\N-How did you have it?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.04,0:45:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I wanted to see you\Nwalk down the aisle.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.42,0:45:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted, um,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:39.50,0:45:40.42,Default,,0,0,0,,to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:45.38,0:45:46.63,Default,,0,0,0,,May we hug now?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.96,0:45:48.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:55.63,0:45:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I have other matters to attend to.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.67,0:46:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Namely, the kidnap of my favorite child.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.13,0:46:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,-Favorite?\N-Mm. Have you met Sherlock?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.71,0:46:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Glorious in combat, but what a mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.67,0:46:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it is up to you to find him.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.00,0:46:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You do not think me capable?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.88,0:46:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,On the contrary.\NI think you're extraordinary.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.63,0:46:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Word of advice, if I may.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.21,0:46:23.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Moriarty has the same brain\Nas your brother's.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.79,0:46:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,So look for what's in front of you, yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.04,0:46:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,but do not forget\Nto look behind that front.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:33.13,0:46:36.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The puzzle is always as devious\Nas the setter.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.29,0:46:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Write that down.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.17,0:46:40.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you tie it?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.46,0:46:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,What was your dress like?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.13,0:46:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Ill-used.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:46.13,0:46:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,And why weren't you at the church?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.83,0:46:53.75,Default,,0,0,0,,-Perhaps a question for another time.\N-Mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.33,0:46:58.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't despair, darling.\NYou learnt the most important thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:59.50,0:47:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock is alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:11.29,0:47:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-They're both alive?\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:13.75,0:47:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,This is all Moriarty?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:16.79,0:47:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:18.08,0:47:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,All along.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.50,0:47:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And you nearly died?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:24.00,0:47:26.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I fell for her trap.\NTwice, Tewkesbury. Twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.88,0:47:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-You were…\N-That's so unlike me.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:28.75,0:47:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You were brave.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.54,0:47:39.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:40.83,0:47:42.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-I… I can manage. It's all right.\N-I insist.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.75,0:47:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:57.17,0:47:58.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Wh…
Dialogue: 0,0:48:01.08,0:48:02.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you so good to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:05.50,0:48:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I'm choosing to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.83,0:48:13.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You're all I have, Enola.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:14.17,0:48:15.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm not going to lose you.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.04,0:48:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that a bathing cabin?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:31.75,0:48:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:34.13,0:48:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola, did--
Dialogue: 0,0:48:35.88,0:48:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Take off your shoes. You'll slip.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.46,0:48:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I have never been in one of these.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:48.08,0:48:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,All so that a woman\Ncould take a swim in the sea.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.58,0:48:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Shall we take a swim?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:01.17,0:50:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I missed you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.58,0:50:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Me too.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:33.54,0:50:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I was never\Nforcing you into this marriage?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.33,0:50:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.25,0:50:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I was never saying,\N"You must marry me," was I?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.63,0:50:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,When I said yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:53.04,0:50:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I said yes to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.54,0:50:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And then it felt like\Neveryone was crowding in
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.88,0:51:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,with what I must say and how I must behave\Nand who I should invite and…
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.25,0:51:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:05.50,0:51:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I started to feel I wasn't enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.71,0:51:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But any doubt was never of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:14.67,0:51:16.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Never of spending my life with you or
Dialogue: 0,0:51:18.21,0:51:19.67,Default,,0,0,0,,committing to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:30.42,0:51:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.50,0:51:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I know I hurt you terribly.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.63,0:51:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.96,0:52:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Drink.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:20.75,0:52:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I could get used to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.33,0:52:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Give her water.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:29.08,0:52:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I will quench her\Nafter I am done with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.67,0:52:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I say,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.96,0:52:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,here's fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.17,0:52:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you tell me what I'm planning?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:44.17,0:52:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I've left enough clues.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.21,0:52:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:49.83,0:52:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You came to Malta a year ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.21,0:52:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I suspect at the behest\Nof someone in power
Dialogue: 0,0:52:55.63,0:52:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,who could have negotiated\Nyour early release from prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.38,0:53:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe you contrived to bring\Nmy sister here and her wedding here.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:03.00,0:53:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,How, I do not know.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.21,0:53:08.63,Default,,0,0,0,,But impressively, you accomplished it.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.71,0:53:11.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, perhaps\Nyou should ask your cellmate.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.54,0:53:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And how easy you were\Nto manipulate, Lady Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.21,0:53:21.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Wanting your exotic wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.17,0:53:24.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Remind me,\Nwhere did you and your husband marry?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.58,0:53:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Malta.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.04,0:53:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:33.58,0:53:34.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.83,0:53:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Masterful stroke.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:37.08,0:53:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,That's high praise from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.13,0:53:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,When we got to the island,\Nyou set a stone rolling down a slope.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.67,0:53:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You kidnapped me to make Enola
Dialogue: 0,0:53:46.63,0:53:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,perform for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:48.13,0:53:51.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So I trap you in order to make her work.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:51.25,0:53:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would I do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:52.50,0:53:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Because you know she cares.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:56.92,0:53:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That is not the question.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:00.00,0:54:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola is behaving rationally.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:02.38,0:54:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,She is doing all she can\Nto right this situation, whereas you…
Dialogue: 0,0:54:07.08,0:54:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it in service to others? No.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.71,0:54:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You never truly work for others,\Nor with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:11.92,0:54:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,They believe you do,\Nbut then you just do away with them
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.42,0:54:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,as soon as their purpose is served.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:17.92,0:54:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it an act of revenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:20.71,0:54:21.67,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:22.63,0:54:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Far too base for Professor Moriarty.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:26.50,0:54:28.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I mention I met your mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:29.67,0:54:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,She blows up a post office,\Nand you celebrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.29,0:54:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.33,0:54:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet I steal from the truly corrupt,\Nand you watch me carted to prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.88,0:54:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:42.96,0:54:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,This is an anger with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:44.71,0:54:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My anger is with hypocrisy.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:47.83,0:54:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,My boredom is with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:50.50,0:54:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Your suppositions are moderate.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.54,0:54:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I expected better.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.54,0:54:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I played your game.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:01.04,0:55:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You promised her water.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.13,0:55:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.58,0:55:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I need little from you…
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.13,0:55:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and less from her.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:53.33,0:55:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Worry not.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:55.92,0:55:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no great thirst.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:58.92,0:56:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not worry, Lady Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:02.92,0:56:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola will succeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:15.33,0:56:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,It was Moriarty all along.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.92,0:56:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.67,0:56:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You came here to ruin my family.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:23.96,0:56:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Revenge on us?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.38,0:56:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Far too simple for her, surely?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.67,0:56:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Moriarty has the same brain\Nas your brother's.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.17,0:56:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Look for what's in front of you,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:32.92,0:56:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,but do not forget\Nto look behind that front.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.13,0:56:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,There is more to understand here.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.58,0:56:40.63,Default,,0,0,0,,But what?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:41.71,0:56:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola, are you awake?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:44.58,0:56:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-I've had a thought.\N-Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:48.38,0:56:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The woman in the purple dress--
Dialogue: 0,0:56:49.79,0:56:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The family\Nyou're marrying into are intolerable.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.58,0:56:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,This woman gave me a bedpan,\Nthought I was her maid.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.04,0:56:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:56.50,0:56:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! Aha, son-in-law.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:59.33,0:57:01.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, almost. Uh, back together?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:03.33,0:57:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh…
Dialogue: 0,0:57:04.58,0:57:07.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I quite agree, by the way.\NMy family are rather intolerable.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:07.88,0:57:09.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-Earnest.\N-Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.21,0:57:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Eudoria Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:11.29,0:57:13.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-It's an honor.\N-I like him.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.25,0:57:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you like a bedpan?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:15.83,0:57:17.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.21,0:57:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, daughter, have you found a thread\Nthat is worth pulling on?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:21.29,0:57:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We are all out of morphine and bandages.\NI'm quite exhausted.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.00,0:57:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Please tell me we're close\Non finding Sherlock.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:26.54,0:57:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You must be Dr. Watson.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.25,0:57:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Eudoria Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:30.46,0:57:31.46,Default,,0,0,0,,A… a great pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.54,0:57:34.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Two handsome men in a tent.\NWe are very lucky.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.38,0:57:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you wish to say everything\Nthat comes to your mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.92,0:57:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.25,0:57:41.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson,\NI feel we are getting closer to Sherlock,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.96,0:57:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,but I have no firm leads,\Nand I need time to think.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:45.04,0:57:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-We'd do better to let you sit alone.\N-Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.21,0:57:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,When Sherlock's deducing,\Nhe prefers complete silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:50.50,0:57:52.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock is a bore.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:52.17,0:57:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,A little discussion I don't think\Nis gonna hurt Enola's thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.21,0:57:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,-I--\N-I have a thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:56.71,0:57:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-Three men. It's an avalanche.\N-Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:58.75,0:58:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I apologize. I was close at hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.29,0:58:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you were listening in.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:02.21,0:58:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-Do you know how loud you all are?\N-Who's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:04.67,0:58:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,My name is Mikiel Mizzi\Nof the Partito Anti-Riformista.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:09.33,0:58:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,"We wish to be rid of your Crown."
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.79,0:58:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And you want a free Malta.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:12.17,0:58:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Actually, I'd like everyone to leave.\N-I can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:14.58,0:58:17.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, I fear\Nthere is something you have missed.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.83,0:58:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The woman in the purple dress.\NAll right? Her hat.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:21.13,0:58:22.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Her hat was from Garrett & Co.'s.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.88,0:58:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. And this year's style.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:29.58,0:58:30.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Good for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:31.21,0:58:34.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes, uh, that…\NUh, sorry, that is a society hat.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:35.88,0:58:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Money had been invested\Ninto making her fit into polite society.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:40.33,0:58:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It is my contention that woman was not\NMoriarty's assassin, nor a soldier,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:44.21,0:58:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,but Moriarty's spy.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:46.92,0:58:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-A good suggestion, Tewkesbury.\N-Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:49.25,0:58:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,If we can figure out\Nwho she was spying on,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:52.29,0:58:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,if she was indeed working for Moriarty,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.54,0:58:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,then the question of her motive\Nmight become easier to answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:59.46,0:59:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me think.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:01.67,0:59:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,She was speaking with two men\Nbefore the carnival.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:05.00,0:59:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,One was the governor,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:07.42,0:59:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,but the other one,\Nhe was wearing a fox mask
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.67,0:59:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,and medals.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:14.75,0:59:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The brigadier.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.92,0:59:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would he be talking to Moriarty's spy?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:23.13,0:59:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury, where are those medals\NI gave you?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:25.67,0:59:26.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh…
Dialogue: 0,0:59:33.58,0:59:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,He was wearing this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:35.79,0:59:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the same one\Nthe soldier at the banquet was wearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:38.79,0:59:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Please be upstanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:45.71,0:59:46.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Afghanistan.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:47.29,0:59:48.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's from the Anglo-Afghan War.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:49.00,0:59:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It was given to those who saw conflict
Dialogue: 0,0:59:51.04,0:59:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-in the Battle of Khost.\N-Khost.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:53.75,0:59:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Khost.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:55.33,0:59:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,My father fought with my godfather\Nin the Battle of Khost.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:58.21,1:00:00.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-The brigadier?\N-We need to speak to him.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:00.33,1:00:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,How do we speak to him?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.58,1:00:02.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:07.04,1:00:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,These military men\Nare very good at busily saying nothing.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.58,1:00:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The brigadier's office\Nis this way. Follow me, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:15.13,1:00:17.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No. We need to do as Moriarty was.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.83,1:00:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We need to be a bit devious.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:21.08,1:00:24.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, who here… is good at that?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:34.71,1:00:35.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Incoming.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:37.96,1:00:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,-There you are.\N-That was easier with younger bones.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:40.42,1:00:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Here. All right, come on.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:42.25,1:00:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You must walk ahead. I will stay\Nbehind you as your man-servant.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.29,1:00:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:46.21,1:00:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Far be it from me\Nto explain the colonies to a colonizer.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:49.79,1:00:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sadly, no one here will understand
Dialogue: 0,1:00:52.67,1:00:55.83,Default,,0,0,0,,a man from his country\Nwalking beside women from ours.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:55.92,1:00:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,-Mother, what's the plan?\N-We'll be posh. Don't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:59.29,1:01:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You're discussing this now?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:00.46,1:01:02.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We are discussing this now, sir.\NBecause this is important.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:02.92,1:01:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you bring a floor plan?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:05.08,1:01:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon, madam.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:08.08,1:01:09.75,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on? Can I help you?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.38,1:01:13.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.\NYes, hello. Just the man I want.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.17,1:01:16.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Could you show us\Nthe way to the records room?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:16.13,1:01:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,-Recor…\N-The records room.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:17.92,1:01:20.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. I've been sent by the brigadier.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:20.33,1:01:21.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Brigadier Sampson.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:21.96,1:01:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,To surprise, uh, my… my…\Nmy husband, Colonel Remington.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:26.04,1:01:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Remington.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:27.25,1:01:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Remington.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:29.33,1:01:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not know the name.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:32.13,1:01:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,-Really?\N-No.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:35.54,1:01:36.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you quite sure of that?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:37.29,1:01:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Y… yes, ma'am, I… I know him.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:39.88,1:01:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,L… let me… Let me show you him…\NRecords room, you say?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:44.25,1:01:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.17,1:01:48.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not forget one led\Nthe life of a lady before one fled.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.54,1:01:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I… I'm sorry.\NI have no news of your mother.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:54.21,1:01:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-Oh.\N-But the concern is palpable. I have…
Dialogue: 0,1:01:56.54,1:01:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,-Everything I have is out there searching.\N-Thank you for your efforts.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:59.92,1:02:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I am actually here\Nfor a different reason, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:01.83,1:02:05.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I hoped to ask you\Nabout a city called Khost.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.79,1:02:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Khost. Yes, I think I know it.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:10.79,1:02:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You were there with my father.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:12.08,1:02:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,In the Anglo-Afghan war.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:13.54,1:02:16.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Khost, I remember it, yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:17.38,1:02:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I'm so sorry. How rude. You are?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:19.67,1:02:21.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:21.79,1:02:23.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Captain Watson. I served in Ashanti.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:25.00,1:02:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,A testing time.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:26.71,1:02:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:31.04,1:02:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You all right there, darling?\NWe must move quickly before he wakes.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:40.79,1:02:41.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do we begin?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:42.96,1:02:44.38,Default,,0,0,0,,We read, darling.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:45.21,1:02:46.33,Default,,0,0,0,,We read.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:48.42,1:02:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything relating to Khost\Nor the Anglo-Afghan war.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:52.13,1:02:56.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord Tewkesbury, Sr., spoke with me\Nat length of what happened at Khost.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:56.96,1:02:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,-So, you knew Peter?\N-Oh yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:59.08,1:03:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And Peter told me he wished for his son\Nto be a part of the solution.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:04.46,1:03:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not like\Nthe tone of this conversation.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:07.33,1:03:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,We come seeking your help.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:10.04,1:03:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We feel there is a threat\Ntowards the people of Malta.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:13.63,1:03:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,And we need to know what you know
Dialogue: 0,1:03:16.67,1:03:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,of what happened in Khost.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.00,1:03:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me, there are some things\Nyou don't need to know about, boy.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:21.88,1:03:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I know what can happen in battle.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:26.75,1:03:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The lines that can be crossed.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:28.71,1:03:32.58,Default,,0,0,0,,An army medic,\Neven at the rank of captain,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:33.38,1:03:34.83,Default,,0,0,0,,does not understand the decision--
Dialogue: 0,1:03:34.92,1:03:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It was my job\Nto pull the dead from the field.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:39.83,1:03:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I faced bullets. I took them.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:43.75,1:03:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Have no doubt\NI understand the consequences.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:59.33,1:04:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Khost.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:02.21,1:04:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I found it.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:09.08,1:04:10.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:11.04,1:04:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, these files, they have been damaged.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.17,1:04:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, pages ripped.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:14.88,1:04:18.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever it is, it has permeated\Nfar deeper than we thought.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:18.46,1:04:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Look… at the indentations.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:21.75,1:04:23.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I can retrace these.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:24.00,1:04:26.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother, do you have a pen…cil?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:26.17,1:04:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:38.17,1:04:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:42.46,1:04:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,He's fine.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.04,1:04:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:46.46,1:04:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,There were British\Nand Maltese soldiers in the battle.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:51.13,1:04:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,"Mission complete.\NDeath toll incalculable."
Dialogue: 0,1:04:55.46,1:04:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,"Reparations, one tonne Afghan gold."
Dialogue: 0,1:04:59.00,1:05:02.46,Default,,0,0,0,,"Locals labeled it 'cleansing.'\NIt was theft."
Dialogue: 0,1:05:05.33,1:05:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Moriarty knows about the gold.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:09.04,1:05:10.08,Default,,0,0,0,,But how?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:11.42,1:05:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sergeant N. Smith.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:14.00,1:05:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:16.25,1:05:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,He was her inside man.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:18.71,1:05:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, this is horrible.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:20.42,1:05:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the answers we receive\Nare rarely the answers we seek.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:28.25,1:05:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, my darling.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:29.96,1:05:33.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We criminals, we've taken you\Nas far as we can.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:33.63,1:05:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-Pencil?\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.17,1:05:37.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, on you go. Make hell.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:41.58,1:05:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-Tewkesbury!\N-I say! I say!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:44.17,1:05:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,They stole!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:45.58,1:05:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,They stole. They looted,\Nand they stole in Khost.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:48.46,1:05:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,-What are you talking about?\N-I recognize who she is and what she is--
Dialogue: 0,1:05:51.29,1:05:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,They killed innocent people,\Nstole gold from a shrine in Afghanistan.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:55.00,1:05:57.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And they did so from the orders\Nof the British government.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:57.50,1:06:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,They brought it here to Malta,\Nand they hid it.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:01.63,1:06:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this true?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:03.54,1:06:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:09.08,1:06:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, sir, my father was a good man.\NYou… you know.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:12.38,1:06:13.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, tell me…
Dialogue: 0,1:06:15.75,1:06:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,he was a good man.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:17.13,1:06:20.50,Default,,0,0,0,,There are practicalities in war\Nthat go beyond the mere morality of good.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:20.58,1:06:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:23.29,1:06:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The British government\Nand the armed forces were at loggerheads.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:26.63,1:06:30.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We were under pressure to reduce costs.\NBut there was no way of reducing costs.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.75,1:06:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,This was war.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:32.75,1:06:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,So the decision was made\Nto right matters by…
Dialogue: 0,1:06:37.63,1:06:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Thievery?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:39.46,1:06:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Murder?\N-No, we saw it as advanced reparations.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:42.71,1:06:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It's established practice after war,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:46.04,1:06:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,for our cost and our loss.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:48.33,1:06:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And what of their losses?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:52.13,1:06:55.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you have to understand\Nthat we were fighting for an empire.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:55.38,1:06:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And some
Dialogue: 0,1:06:57.96,1:06:59.29,Default,,0,0,0,,miscalculations were made.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:59.38,1:07:00.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Miscalculations?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:02.00,1:07:05.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Miscalculations? Where is your honor?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:08.21,1:07:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, sir,\Nwhat was my father's role in this?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:12.63,1:07:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Was he told to do this?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:18.50,1:07:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Your father loved you.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:20.67,1:07:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Immensely.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:26.50,1:07:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The operation…
Dialogue: 0,1:07:30.67,1:07:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,was his.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:35.96,1:07:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Excuse me.\N-Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:37.50,1:07:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:39.00,1:07:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:02.29,1:08:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My father was a soldier as well.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:08.13,1:08:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,A loyal servant of the British Raj.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:13.08,1:08:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,He loved the Crown.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:15.88,1:08:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Believed in its right to rule India.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:19.79,1:08:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And I thought he was right to do so.\NI was a child.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:22.83,1:08:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,He was my hero.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.17,1:08:26.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The gold, what happened to it?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:28.88,1:08:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You do understand what could happen\Nto Lady Tewkesbury and Sherlock
Dialogue: 0,1:08:31.96,1:08:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,if you say nothing?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:33.17,1:08:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the… The gold was transported here.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:36.08,1:08:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:37.75,1:08:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It was to be produced\Nas though Malta was where it was found,
Dialogue: 0,1:08:40.88,1:08:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,or, in fact, where it was taken.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.83,1:08:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But it never returned to Britain.\NAm I right?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:47.04,1:08:49.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Peter had a crisis of conscience.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:50.17,1:08:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Took me until the Ashanti to realize\Nthe damage our Crown had done.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.13,1:08:58.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The way we treated the people brutally.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:59.54,1:09:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I suddenly saw it so clearly.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:03.08,1:09:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I suppose I saw him clearly.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:05.29,1:09:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,As we returned to Malta,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:07.67,1:09:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,he waited for his men to come to land,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:09.67,1:09:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and then he sunk the ship
Dialogue: 0,1:09:11.75,1:09:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and claimed that the gold\Nwent down with it.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:13.83,1:09:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,-He should have returned the gold.\N-No.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:16.83,1:09:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No, my dear, the British Empire,\Nit cannot admit guilt.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:20.54,1:09:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,And the embarrassment…
Dialogue: 0,1:09:21.63,1:09:24.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Such was the rage\Namongst our senior officers, that we…
Dialogue: 0,1:09:24.42,1:09:26.83,Default,,0,0,0,,we feared for our careers, so we…
Dialogue: 0,1:09:27.42,1:09:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,we blamed the Maltese soldiers\Nin our unit. Said it was a mutiny.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:31.96,1:09:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,We allowed them\Nto take the fall for the missing gold.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:36.29,1:09:37.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We are all made,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:38.21,1:09:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,but the truth… makes us in turn.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:45.75,1:09:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,More than our heroes.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:49.63,1:09:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,More than our fathers.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:57.08,1:09:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I always thought my father a great man.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:59.92,1:10:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Many men get distracted\Nby what it means to be great
Dialogue: 0,1:10:02.42,1:10:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,and lose themselves in the process.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:04.25,1:10:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,But to be capable\Nof such horrendous things…
Dialogue: 0,1:10:06.50,1:10:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't make it any better for you,\NLord Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:13.58,1:10:18.04,Default,,0,0,0,,All I can tell you is,\Nyou needn't walk the same path.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:19.83,1:10:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is the gold now?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:21.46,1:10:22.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I don't know, do I?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:24.13,1:10:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,He didn't want me\Nto hold responsibility for it.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:27.83,1:10:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Peter said that it was pirate gold
Dialogue: 0,1:10:29.75,1:10:32.58,Default,,0,0,0,,and that he didn't want me\Nto be tarnished by it, and I was…
Dialogue: 0,1:10:33.71,1:10:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Pirate gold?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:38.50,1:10:39.54,Default,,0,0,0,,See that cave?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:40.04,1:10:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,He told me when I was a boy\Nthat there was treasure hidden inside.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:43.83,1:10:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:46.75,1:10:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:48.46,1:10:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,With Moriarty, it's never just one thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:50.83,1:10:54.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Why shouldn't I have a share\Nof your ill-begotten riches
Dialogue: 0,1:10:54.75,1:10:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,and punish you at the same time?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:57.00,1:11:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,She wants to wrong us,\Nbut she also wants the stolen riches.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:01.50,1:11:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I know where the gold is, but she doesn't.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:04.38,1:11:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Who?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:05.42,1:11:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-The puzzle is as devious as the setter.\N-The puzzle is as devious as the setter.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:09.00,1:11:10.63,Default,,0,0,0,,How could I have missed this?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:10.71,1:11:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I should have known it\Nfrom the moment she tried to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:16.38,1:11:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,She should have killed me.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:19.83,1:11:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It would have protected her identity.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:22.38,1:11:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I agree that would be useful.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:25.54,1:11:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a goose chase.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:27.00,1:11:29.04,Default,,0,0,0,,A constructed goose chase.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:29.13,1:11:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,She laid the traps, and we fell for them.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:32.17,1:11:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:33.21,1:11:34.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The discoveries.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:35.92,1:11:38.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock and Lady Tewkesbury's abductions.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:40.29,1:11:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The fire at the hotel.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:42.50,1:11:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm entirely lost\Nas to what is happening here.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:45.29,1:11:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be surprised\Nif she was held responsible
Dialogue: 0,1:11:48.17,1:11:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,for the smudges of Morse code\Non his mirror.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:56.25,1:11:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The only missing piece that we had\Nwas Tewkesbury's father.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:59.33,1:12:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,A… and she knew of Khost,\Nand she knew of he.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:03.83,1:12:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And she knows Tewkesbury loves me.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:06.21,1:12:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And only Tewkesbury could bring me to him.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:08.29,1:12:09.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-Me?\N-Yes, you.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:09.25,1:12:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And you could bring me
Dialogue: 0,1:12:11.75,1:12:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,to the gold.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:19.42,1:12:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,She has led us every step of the way.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:22.58,1:12:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:26.17,1:12:27.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:33.33,1:12:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury, I have…
Dialogue: 0,1:12:35.13,1:12:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,-I have solved the case.\N-You have?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:39.13,1:12:40.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And I have a plan.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:46.33,1:12:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Moriarty has spun her web,
Dialogue: 0,1:12:48.58,1:12:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,and now I must fly into it.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:59.33,1:13:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You thinking what I'm thinking?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:03.71,1:13:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:05.42,1:13:06.58,Default,,0,0,0,,She is watching us somewhere,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:06.67,1:13:09.17,Default,,0,0,0,,but she does not know\Nwhere the gold is yet.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:09.67,1:13:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I will take her there.\NYou know what to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:11.88,1:13:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Stay here.\N-What if she's hiding deeper in the cave?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:18.67,1:13:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:21.17,1:13:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,this is a good plan.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:23.58,1:13:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,If she is there, I will deal with her.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:29.04,1:13:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:35.08,1:14:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, get away!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:57.63,1:16:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:07.25,1:17:08.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:13.58,1:17:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:33.54,1:17:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's my brother?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:34.79,1:17:37.50,Default,,0,0,0,,He will be released\Nas soon as I have what I need.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:37.58,1:17:40.46,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we trust you?\NI have seen two dead by your hands.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:41.63,1:17:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Always so superior.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:44.25,1:17:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Must you protect gold\Nthat is filthy with blood?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:49.58,1:17:50.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Stained you,
Dialogue: 0,1:17:51.38,1:17:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,as it has stained that floppy boy\Nwhose dirty name you almost took.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:56.29,1:17:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But then what of the Holmes name?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:00.38,1:18:03.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder what privilege that is built on.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:03.42,1:18:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:05.33,1:18:08.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Sugar? From Jamaica, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:08.96,1:18:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Silk or cotton from India?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:13.46,1:18:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,There are few British names\Nthat are not tarnished
Dialogue: 0,1:18:16.46,1:18:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,with the pain of its empire.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:40.29,1:18:42.33,Default,,0,0,0,,There are 20 more boxes inside.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:43.67,1:18:46.04,Default,,0,0,0,,There. You have the gold.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:46.13,1:18:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Now where is my brother?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:48.71,1:18:51.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You and your heart.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:51.67,1:18:56.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you really think I would\Nhand him over to you so easily?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:57.33,1:19:02.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not allow you or your brother\Nto foil my plans for another moment.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:03.42,1:19:08.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again,\Nyou are behind the curve, Miss Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:10.96,1:19:12.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you quite sure of that?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:14.75,1:19:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You are surrounded!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:19.79,1:19:22.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You are not the only one\Nwith friends in Malta, Professor.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:28.13,1:19:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Drop your weapons!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:12.33,1:20:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-Now!\N-Enola!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:24.00,1:20:25.21,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:25.75,1:20:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:27.08,1:20:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-No!\N-Enola, wait!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:28.00,1:20:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:39.42,1:20:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Hyah!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:50.83,1:20:51.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Hyah!
Dialogue: 0,1:21:32.00,1:21:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Help! Help!
Dialogue: 0,1:21:35.54,1:21:36.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We're in here!
Dialogue: 0,1:21:39.63,1:21:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I love you.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:41.21,1:21:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,She's full of this fight.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:42.21,1:22:43.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock!
Dialogue: 0,1:22:43.88,1:22:46.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock! Sherlock! Sherlock.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:47.92,1:22:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Free her! Free her, Enola!
Dialogue: 0,1:22:50.46,1:22:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:55.17,1:22:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:01.54,1:23:03.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry if this hurts.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:04.25,1:23:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-No.\N-I'll be back. Breathe.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:12.25,1:23:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,There!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:13.33,1:23:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,There, there, there!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:14.71,1:23:16.04,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:16.13,1:23:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,No! No, no, no!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:18.96,1:23:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Shooting you would make a dull end.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:26.88,1:23:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You baited me.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:30.29,1:23:31.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm impressed.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:32.29,1:23:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you made it easy.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:34.96,1:23:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You're so unlike your brother.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:40.42,1:23:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He shows me nothing.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:43.92,1:23:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But you?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:51.17,1:23:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You're so
Dialogue: 0,1:23:53.83,1:23:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,emotional!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:56.50,1:23:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You're being emotional.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:59.00,1:24:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It's understandable,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:00.96,1:24:02.29,Default,,0,0,0,,but unnecessary.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:08.42,1:24:11.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I find it quite understandable…
Dialogue: 0,1:24:14.67,1:24:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and very, very necessary.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:26.96,1:24:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Days.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:33.21,1:24:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Days.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:36.46,1:24:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:38.04,1:24:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me…
Dialogue: 0,1:24:41.71,1:24:42.88,Default,,0,0,0,,why I should not.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.96,1:24:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not us.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:44.25,1:24:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not what we believe in.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:46.83,1:24:50.04,Default,,0,0,0,,If we give her to the police,\Nshe'll just escape again.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:51.75,1:24:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,She'll come after us again.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:54.96,1:24:56.38,Default,,0,0,0,,And this whole
Dialogue: 0,1:24:58.29,1:25:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,bloody affair… will be on repeat.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:03.13,1:25:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And repeat.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:06.29,1:25:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,And repeat.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:07.67,1:25:08.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:08.83,1:25:10.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:11.08,1:25:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Sherlock, look at me, please!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:13.25,1:25:14.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't do this.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:25.58,1:25:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Think.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:28.46,1:25:30.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You're being emotional.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:07.29,1:26:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been given word that Moriarty\Nwill be transported back to Blighty
Dialogue: 0,1:26:10.96,1:26:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,with no chance of escape.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:12.92,1:26:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, the gold will be traveling\Nback to Afghanistan with Dr. Watson and I,
Dialogue: 0,1:26:17.46,1:26:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,where it will be returned\Nto those it was stolen from.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:19.58,1:26:21.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to Lord Tewkesbury,\NI have been granted responsibility
Dialogue: 0,1:26:22.00,1:26:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,to undertake investigations.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:23.75,1:26:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We intend to prosecute all those\Ninvolved in crimes on Maltese soil.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:26.67,1:26:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Moriarty's actions exposed a great wrong.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:30.00,1:26:33.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The time may have even come\Nfor Malta to be free of the British.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:33.83,1:26:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:35.33,1:26:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, you might be right about that.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:42.42,1:26:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you understand\Nwhy I had to do this.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:45.54,1:26:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Your father would be so proud of you.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:51.21,1:26:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it time?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:01.21,1:27:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,For Queen and country
Dialogue: 0,1:27:04.96,1:27:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and all that that means.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:24.42,1:27:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,She was brave.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:27.67,1:27:30.88,Default,,0,0,0,,She had a resilience at times\Nthat I did not.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:30.96,1:27:33.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Moriarty saw that, tried to stamp it out.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:34.96,1:27:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet I think she did not succeed.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.04,1:27:38.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Share.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.96,1:27:40.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Share.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:40.54,1:27:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Your notebooks.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:42.33,1:27:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,They were not easy to decipher.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:46.33,1:27:49.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you think I would have hope\Nof deciphering yours?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:50.54,1:27:51.96,Default,,0,0,0,,We are siblings,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:52.54,1:27:56.04,Default,,0,0,0,,but our notebooks,\Nlike our minds, are our own.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:56.83,1:27:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, indeed.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:58.63,1:28:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And your mind, Enola,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:02.04,1:28:04.04,Default,,0,0,0,,is one I admire hugely.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:06.00,1:28:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:11.08,1:28:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you for everything.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:15.08,1:28:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,For I…
Dialogue: 0,1:28:23.00,1:28:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I forgot myself.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:28.25,1:28:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You remembered soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:30.63,1:28:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You think you know fear,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:33.29,1:28:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,then suddenly,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:35.46,1:28:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,you're in a dark place…
Dialogue: 0,1:28:39.33,1:28:40.96,Default,,0,0,0,,with someone that you cannot protect.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:45.50,1:28:48.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. Watson was there…\N…fighting for you too.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:48.67,1:28:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:53.83,1:28:55.04,Default,,0,0,0,,He's a good man.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:55.13,1:28:57.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And Tewkesbury, he has more\Nthan I thought about him.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:57.88,1:28:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. He's worth something.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:00.67,1:29:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And Mother, of course.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:02.54,1:29:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Her, I'm not so sure about.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:07.29,1:29:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What I said
Dialogue: 0,1:29:09.71,1:29:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,in our
Dialogue: 0,1:29:11.75,1:29:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,disagreement--
Dialogue: 0,1:29:12.67,1:29:15.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It… it's all right. Consider it forgotten.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:15.42,1:29:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I… I said things I didn't mean too.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:17.29,1:29:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:20.71,1:29:22.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:23.38,1:29:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,But what I failed to say…
Dialogue: 0,1:29:28.54,1:29:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,is that truly…
Dialogue: 0,1:29:33.25,1:29:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,you are so much more.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:38.13,1:29:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You might even be
Dialogue: 0,1:29:40.29,1:29:41.38,Default,,0,0,0,,extraordinary.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:53.83,1:29:56.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Though I do not know when you grew so old.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:57.71,1:29:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Turns out,\NI've been getting older every day.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:59.79,1:30:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:03.29,1:30:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You have.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:27.75,1:30:31.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I never wanted to marry\Na future Lady of Tewkesbury. I…
Dialogue: 0,1:30:32.04,1:30:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But I do wish to be your husband.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:38.42,1:30:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not wish to take your name.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:40.04,1:30:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Nor would I.\NMy name is tarnished beyond all measure.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:44.00,1:30:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I mean… your title.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:47.88,1:30:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm giving up my title.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:50.79,1:30:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm in the process of… of resigning it.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:53.92,1:30:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be a lord no more.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:55.54,1:30:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:56.58,1:30:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take on our blood name, Tebbity-Gore.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:02.29,1:31:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Tebbity…
Dialogue: 0,1:31:03.54,1:31:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Tebbity-Gore?\N-Tewkesbury is my given name.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:05.58,1:31:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Viscount Tewkesbury,\Nthe Marquess of Basilwether.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:09.38,1:31:12.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But, yeah, my…\Nmy real name is… is Tebbity-Gore.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:14.96,1:31:16.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't like it, do you?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:18.88,1:31:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Tewkesbury is my favorite.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:22.42,1:31:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,But I don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:24.54,1:31:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,All I've ever wanted\Nwas for you to be you,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:27.33,1:31:28.79,Default,,0,0,0,,and for me to be me.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:28.88,1:31:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:32.96,1:31:34.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Earnest Tebbity…
Dialogue: 0,1:31:35.38,1:31:37.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-It just hurts to say.\N-It's bad, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:37.58,1:31:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Does it feel right for you?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:47.38,1:31:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I made a mistake with what I said\Nat the beginning of this tale.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:51.96,1:31:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,As it turns out, I misunderstood.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:56.17,1:31:58.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not that good stories\Nbegin with a wedding.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:00.38,1:32:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:01.96,1:32:03.42,Default,,0,0,0,,They end with one.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:09.75,1:32:11.63,Default,,0,0,0,,-You look beautiful.\N-Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:13.58,1:32:14.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you like being married?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:15.67,1:32:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I married the wrong man.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:18.92,1:32:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you're pairing yourself\Nwith the right one.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:21.58,1:32:22.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:24.17,1:32:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And now,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:26.33,1:32:28.08,Default,,0,0,0,,in the spirit of great partnership…
Dialogue: 0,1:32:28.17,1:32:30.79,Default,,0,0,0,,-Mm-hmm?\N-The matter of your wedding gift.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:30.88,1:32:31.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh dear.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:31.79,1:32:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought of jewels,\Nand I thought of books,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:34.54,1:32:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and I thought of paintings, flowers,
Dialogue: 0,1:32:37.46,1:32:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,um, and I decided upon…
Dialogue: 0,1:32:40.67,1:32:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:42.46,1:32:43.29,Default,,0,0,0,,'Tis I.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:46.58,1:32:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Edith. What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:50.00,1:32:54.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Your mother sent me a telegram.\NTold me I must find my way here.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:54.38,1:32:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Though she is little, she is fierce.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:57.08,1:32:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Your name…
Dialogue: 0,1:32:59.29,1:33:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:01.08,1:33:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm, um…
Dialogue: 0,1:33:02.79,1:33:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I'm glad
Dialogue: 0,1:33:04.25,1:33:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,it hasn't limited you.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:06.33,1:33:08.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, yes, "alone" backwards.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:08.63,1:33:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What a curse to give\Nto your only daughter.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:13.46,1:33:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I love my name, Mother.\NI love all of my name.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:17.25,1:33:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola Eudoria Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:21.04,1:33:22.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I will still be a Holmes.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:22.54,1:33:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, sadly, my darling,\Nwe are all still tarred with that brush.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:28.29,1:33:29.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll see you down there.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:38.50,1:33:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Viscount Tewkesbury,\Nthe Marquess of Basilwether.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:41.75,1:33:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a nincompoop.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:42.92,1:33:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Shall we, um, stick together?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:45.50,1:33:47.83,Default,,0,0,0,,-People don't seem to want us, do they?\N-No.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:48.42,1:33:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,At least we've got each other.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:51.63,1:33:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Look into my eyes.\NThe rhythm is always there.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:55.58,1:33:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I can feel it.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:02.33,1:34:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,That message with the fan at the ball,\Nwhat did it mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:05.17,1:34:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It means I love you.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:11.25,1:34:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I have something for you.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:16.08,1:34:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Enola, did you understand what I said?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:18.21,1:34:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You love me.\NAnd as it turns out, I love you too.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:26.13,1:34:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Oi! Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:29.42,1:34:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's begin.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:31.79,1:34:33.33,Default,,0,0,0,,-Hello.\N-Hi.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:34.08,1:34:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I am Mikiel Mizzi\Nof the Partito Anti-Riformista.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:39.96,1:34:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,We believe in a free Malta.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:42.71,1:34:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:44.92,1:34:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,We wish to be rid of your--
Dialogue: 0,1:34:46.04,1:34:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-Okay, listen to the wedding.\N-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:54.25,1:34:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my darling.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:56.83,1:34:59.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I can see how you look at Enola,
Dialogue: 0,1:35:00.25,1:35:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,and I can see how she looks at you.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:03.88,1:35:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish you the greatest happiness.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:09.42,1:35:10.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Thank you.\N-I love you.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:13.13,1:35:15.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:16.13,1:35:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:17.88,1:35:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, dearly beloved,
Dialogue: 0,1:35:21.88,1:35:23.88,Default,,0,0,0,,uh, new family…
Dialogue: 0,1:35:25.17,1:35:26.29,Default,,0,0,0,,…welcome.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:27.21,1:35:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We are gathered here today
Dialogue: 0,1:35:29.25,1:35:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,for the partnership of Earnest and Enola.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:35.33,1:35:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll be a simple ceremony
Dialogue: 0,1:35:37.38,1:35:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,because I really don't know\Nmuch of the original by heart.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:42.46,1:35:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-Rings. Who has the rings?\N-Ah.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:45.79,1:35:46.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:50.38,1:35:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:54.00,1:35:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Right. Ready?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:56.67,1:35:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:58.38,1:35:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Earnest,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:00.96,1:36:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,will you… care for Enola?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:04.79,1:36:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you be a companion to her?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:07.63,1:36:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And will you love her
Dialogue: 0,1:36:09.92,1:36:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,as she needs be loved?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:11.04,1:36:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you mind possibly asking her first?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:12.71,1:36:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,She is rather more complicated\Nin this matter than I.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:16.38,1:36:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:20.33,1:36:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Enola--\N-I want to be his.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:24.33,1:36:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:26.25,1:36:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,'Cause I want to be hers.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:33.08,1:36:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:34.71,1:36:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,then, by the power\Nvested in me by, uh, no one at all…
Dialogue: 0,1:36:40.71,1:36:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,…I pronounce thee woman and husband.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:45.50,1:36:48.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You may now kiss the husband.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:50.75,1:37:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Adeline Rathe. Adeline Rathe.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:53.04,1:37:53.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:54.04,1:37:55.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Adeline Rathe.\N-Adeline Rathe.
